      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you elect to expense the chair entirely using Section 179, you should record the full purchase amount as an immediate business expense in QuickBooks. Ensure you use a specific expense account, like \"Office Equipment Expense\" or \"Furniture & Fixtures.\" This allows your profit and loss statement to show the deduction, while your asset tracking remains clear by noting the original purchase. Simply classifying it as an immediate expense instead of tracking it as a depreciable asset is the correct step for that specific election.",
