      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. one more thing though—i've been looking through my bank transactions from last month and i feel like some small amounts are just... missing. like i see the charge but then the balance looks off or certain small miscellaneous fees aren't lining up with what i expected. it's super annoying trying to find where those tiny gaps are coming from. any tips for auditing these little discrepancies so they don't just stay hidden in my books?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To audit those small discrepancies, start by cross-referencing every bank transaction in QuickBooks against your original bank or credit card statements line by line. Look specifically for bank service charges, pending transactions, or recurring micro-payments that may have been overlooked. Running a reconciliation report in QuickBooks against your bank statement is the most thorough way to force every penny to match up. If gaps persist, you may need to investigate any forgotten deposits or timing differences between the bank's processing and your record-keeping.",
